---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { asset } from '../lib/images';
import { LINKEDIN } from '../data/linkedin';
interface Props { headingLevel?: 'h1' | 'h2' }
const { headingLevel = 'h2' } = Astro.props;
const H = headingLevel;
const figures: [string, string][] = [
  ['skai/blur_skymap.png', 'Median seeing across the survey footprint'],
  ['skai/teff_validation.png', 'My effective exposure time against the DES pipeline, 74,323 exposures'],
  ['skai/best_worst_nights.png', 'The best and the worst night, exposure by exposure'],
  ['skai/blur_airmass.png', "Seeing against airmass, the Simpson's paradox"],
];
---
<section id="skai" class="mx-auto max-w-[1280px] px-5 py-24" aria-labelledby="skai-title">
  <H id="skai-title" class={`h2 ${H === 'h1' ? 'text-[48px] md:text-[80px]' : 'text-[40px] md:text-[56px]'}`}>Summer 2026 at the SkAI Institute</H>
  <p class="mt-5 max-w-[860px] text-[20px] leading-[1.4] md:text-2xl">
    An AI telescope scheduler needs a number that says how good a night of observing was. I built one, and tested it on
    every exposure the Dark Energy Survey took from the Blanco 4-metre telescope at Cerro Tololo, Chile, between 2013 and
    2019. I designed, built and validated it myself, advised by Prof. Alex Drlica-Wagner.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-12 border-t border-rule pt-10">
    <div class="max-w-[720px]">
      <p class="text-[15px] text-chalk-dim">SEED Researcher, NSF-Simons AI Institute for the Sky, summer 2026</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-[1.45]">
        A nine-week research program at the intersection of AI and astrophysical data. My pipeline turned the metric into a
        depth map of the whole survey footprint, built from 74,204 exposures across 1,814 sky hexes and cross-validated to within
        0.2%. I presented that map at the program's closing symposium, then at the poster session.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-3 text-[17px]">
        <li><a href={LINKEDIN.spotlight} class="link font-semibold">SkAI's spotlight on my project</a> <span class="text-chalk-dim">on LinkedIn</span></li>
        <li><a href={LINKEDIN.scheduler} class="link font-semibold">The AI scheduler my metric is built for, observing on the Blanco telescope</a> <span class="text-chalk-dim">on LinkedIn</span></li>
        <li><a href={LINKEDIN.cohort} class="link font-semibold">The 2026 SEED cohort</a> <span class="text-chalk-dim">on LinkedIn</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,840px)_1fr]">
    <a href="/skai/poster.pdf" class="group block border border-rule bg-poster">
      <Image src={asset('skai/poster.png')} alt="Poster: A Report Card for the Night Sky. One score for how good a night of observing was, built on Dark Energy Survey exposures." widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1680]} sizes="(min-width: 1320px) 840px, (min-width: 1024px) 62vw, calc(100vw - 40px)" class="block h-auto w-full" loading={H === 'h1' ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} />
      <span class="block px-5 py-3 text-[15px] text-[#cfe3ea] group-hover:text-white">The poster from my SkAI summer. Opens the PDF.</span>
    </a>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
      <div><div class="big text-5xl">74,323</div><p class="mt-2 text-lg leading-snug">exposures scored, the clean survey sample from a 105,889-exposure DES log</p></div>
      <div><div class="big text-5xl">0.952</div><p class="mt-2 text-lg leading-snug">log-correlation between my calibrated effective exposure time and the DES pipeline's own</p></div>
      <div><div class="big text-5xl">615</div><p class="mt-2 text-lg leading-snug">nights scored; the ranking holds under reweighting for most weight sets (Spearman ≥ 0.98)</p></div>
      <p class="text-lg leading-[1.4]">
        One finding: pooled across the survey, seeing looks like it <em>improves</em> as the telescope points lower, which is
        physically backwards. The scheduler preferentially pointed low when conditions were already good, so a reward learned
        from raw logs inherits that bias.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {figures.map(([src, cap]) => (
      <figure class="border border-rule bg-night-2">
        <Image src={asset(src)} alt={cap} widths={[320, 480, 640]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 300px, (min-width: 640px) 50vw, 100vw" class="block aspect-[4/3] h-auto w-full bg-white object-contain p-2" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption class="px-4 py-3 text-[15px] leading-snug text-chalk-dim">{cap}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-x-9 gap-y-3 text-lg font-semibold">
    <a href="/projects/skai-metrics/" class="link">Read the write-up</a>
    <a href="/skai/report/" class="link">Full report</a>
    <a href="/skai/dashboard/" class="link">Interactive dashboard</a>
    <a href="/skai/poster.pdf" class="link">Poster (PDF, 1.4 MB)</a>
    <a href="/skai/working-note-v0.1.pdf" class="link">Working note (PDF, v0.1)</a>
  </div>
</section>
